ment the behavior described in the prompt.\n    return 0;\n}"},"points":150},{"slug":"matrix-chain-minimum-multiplications","title":"Matrix Chain Multiplication Cost","problem_statement":"Implement matrixChainMinimumMultiplications(dimensions: int[]). A chain of matrices has dimensions dimensions[i] by dimensions[i+1]. Return the minimum scalar multiplications needed to compute the full product by choosing parenthesization; matrix order cannot change.","difficulty":"Medium","topic_tags":["Dynamic Programming","Intervals","Optimization"],"constraints":["2 <= dimensions.length <= 100","1 <= dimensions[i] <= 10000","Cost fits signed 64-bit"],"examples":[{"input":"dimensions = [10,30,5,60]","output":"4500"},{"input":"dimensions = [5,10,3]","output":"150"}],"starter_code_by_language":{"JavaScript":"function matrixChainMinimumMultiplications(dimensions) {\n  // Implement the behavior described in the prompt.\n  return 0;\n}","Python":"def matrix_chain_minimum_multiplications(dimensions):\n    # Implement the behavior described in the prompt.\n    return 0","Java":"public static long matrixChainMinimumMultiplications(int[] dimensions) {\n    // Implement the behavior described in the prompt.\n    return 0L;\n}","C++":"long matrixChainMinimumMultiplications(const vector<int>& dimensions) {\n    // Implement the behavior described in the prompt.\n    return 0LL;\n}"},"points":150},{"slug":"burst-balloons-maximum-coins","title":"Maximum Coins from Bursting Balloons","problem_statement":"Implement burstBalloonsMaximumCoins(values: int[]). Burst every balloon exactly once. Bursting balloon i earns its value times the current values of its nearest unburst neighbors, using 1 outside the array. Return the maximum total coins.","difficulty":"Hard","topic_tags":["Dynamic Programming","Intervals","Optimization"],"constraints":["0 <= values.length <= 300","0 <= values[i] <= 100","The result fits signed 64-bit"],"examples":[{"input":"values = [3,1,5,8]","output":"167"},{"input":"values